 "steps": [
  {
   "id": "s0",
   "title": "Read the question",
   "text": "A gas expands from \\( 1 \\) m³ to \\( 2 \\) m³ at **constant atmospheric pressure**. (a) Find the work done by the gas. (b) Show the work on a P–V diagram.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "title": "(a) Formula",
   "text": "Atmospheric pressure is \\( P = 1\\ \\text{atm} = 1.013\\times10^{5} \\) Pa. At constant pressure the work done by the gas is \\( W = P\\,\\Delta V = P(V_2 - V_1) \\).",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "title": "(a) Substitute",
   "text": "\\[ W = 1.013\\times10^{5} \\times (2 - 1) = 1.013\\times10^{5}\\ \\text{J} \\] The work is **positive** because the gas expands.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "title": "(b) Draw the isobar",
   "text": "On the P–V diagram, volume goes on the horizontal axis (1 to 2 m³) and pressure on the vertical axis. Constant pressure is a **horizontal line** at \\( 1.013\\times10^{5} \\) Pa from \\( V = 1 \\) to \\( V = 2 \\) m³.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "title": "(b) Shade the work",
   "text": "The **shaded rectangle** under the line (width \\( 1 \\) m³, height \\( 1.013\\times10^{5} \\) Pa) represents the work done: its area is \\( 1.013\\times10^{5} \\) J.",
   "actions": []
  },
  {
   "id": "s5",
   "title": "Answer",
   "text": "(a) \\( W = 1.013\\times10^{5} \\) J. (b) The work is the area under the isobar.",
   "actions": []
  }
 ],
 "formulas": [
  {
   "title": "Work at constant pressure",
   "tex": "\\role{work}{W} = P\\,(V_2 - V_1)",
   "text": "Area under the isobar on a P–V diagram."
  }
 ],
 "challenges": [
  {
   "id": "c1",
   "type": "number",
   "title": "Now you try",
   "prompt": "A gas expands from **0.5 m³** to **1.5 m³** at a constant **2 × 10⁵ Pa**. What is the work done in kJ?",
